23.8%?  No, you actually _are_ that good.  That doesn't mean you're
necessarily bored to tears, for sure, but I'm still going to note that
the "when to use missiles" skill is something you definitely have down
pat at this point.

There are only two ways to make a game harder when it's been solved as
thoroughly as Nethack has; one is to introduce massive power creep, where 
you add tons of new monsters and tons of new items to combat them.  
That's usually a bad way to go, because you tend to leave the original
game behind in your dust, and you also generally end up with something
far less balanced as a whole.  Witness Slash'EM, which gave in to power 
creep from the very beginning.

The other is to make tweaks as necessary to revitalize unused portions 
of the existing game, like missile weapons; this is the way I've chosen 
to go, because it doesn't leave huge hunks of the game orphaned.  You may 
be a person who'd rather see power creep, but, well, see above.  I
definitely would not.  (FWIW, I _did_ add the "selected ranged weapon"
UI tweak specifically to make it more convenient for the player to use
missiles, and autopickup_exceptions can be configured to pick up your
chosen flung-object... so it's not as bad as all -that-.)

